From: Reid Smythe <rwsmythe@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 20:52:03 -1000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(wp6.3c): build win64 GPL FFmpeg release/9.0 at b204e94e
 without zvbi

Clearwater WP6.3c (docs/briefs/wp6.3c-brief.md in rwsmythe/clearwater), r2.
r1 (branch wp6.3c-nozvbi, 92d0b6a) pinned FFmpeg to the tag n9.0.2 and
failed to compile: BtbN's openapv pin (b4ff698, openapv >= 1.1) changed
oapvm_create to two arguments, and FFmpeg fixed liboapvenc.c on release/9.0
only after the tag (a7502e5, "avcodec/liboapvenc: fix build with openapv
>= 1.1"). r2 pins the release/9.0 commit b204e94e (n9.0.2 + 47 backports).
- scripts.d/50-zvbi.sh: ffbuild_enabled returns 1, so generate.sh emits
  --disable-libzvbi and never builds the stage (zvbi's packet-830.* and
  pdc.* are GPL-2.0-only and cannot be combined into the GPL-3.0 binary).
- build.sh: one added line after the release/9.0 clone,
  git checkout --detach b204e94e90fca64045e9ca7dd44c65678c7eb29e
  (clone --branch cannot take a commit; set -xe fails the build if the
  commit is missing). addins/9.0.sh stays upstream (release/9.0).
- .github/workflows/build.yml: workflow_dispatch only; repository guard
  for this fork; win64 / gpl 9.0 only; release tagged
  ffmpeg-9.0-gb204e94e-nozvbi-<commit>; no Latest / Wiki / Prune / ghcr
  cleanup.
